WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.269
- I said to my colleagues one
day in the editorial room,

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.740 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Why do we seem to have
a double standard?"

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.608
And there was a
terrible silence.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.111 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I realized at that moment
that I'd crossed a line.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.646
I had no idea what the line
was or why I'd crossed it,

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I realized I'd
stopped being one of them,

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.786
and I'd become one of you.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:23.656
(energetic upbeat music)

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.558 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and
this is the Rubin Report

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:29.162 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
as always guys click that
subscribe button on YouTube.

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.331 line:0%
And don't forget to tap
that notification bell.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.533 line:0%
So you're alerted
of our new videos.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.869 line:0%
And joining me today
is a journalist, author

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:39.472
and columnist for The Times
of London, Melanie Phillips,

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:40.840
welcome to the Rubin Report.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.077
- Thanks Dave, very
good to be with you.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.612
- I'm glad to have you.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I mentioned to you
right before we started here

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:49.682
that for about two years,
I've been getting emails

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start position:0%
and tweets and Facebook messages
and all sorts of things.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:56.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
People saying, "You gotta talk
to this Melanie Phillips."

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.957
Now you're in Jerusalem now,

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.226 align:start size:81% position:19%
but you also split
time in London.

00:01:00.226 --> 00:01:03.129
For my American audience
that may not know you,

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.799 align:start size:88% position:13%
can you just do a little
Melanie Phillips 101?

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:09.102 align:start position:0%
A little bio before we get into
the specifics of your work,

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.438
your writing, your speaking,
your books, that sort of thing.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.139
- Sure, sure.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:17.644 line:0%
Well, I am a British Jew,
born and bred in London

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:21.815 align:start size:97% position:3%
of parents who were themselves
born and bred in London.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.751
Had a fairly conventional
upbringing of the type

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.954
that British Jews
in the 1950s had.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
Parents, not very religious,
not very observant,

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.727
but nevertheless belonged
to an Orthodox synagogue.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:38.898
I went to Oxford University
and read English literature,

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:88% position:13%
which fits you for
everything and nothing.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.602
And fell into journalism.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was trained though
in those days,

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:49.375 align:start size:84% position:16%
journalists were
actually trained and
we were taught things

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:88% position:13%
like objectivity, and
the need to be truthful,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.682
and the needs to be factual,

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the need to separate
fact from opinion,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.886
would you believe such a thing?

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:04.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I spent two years learning
all these trade crafts

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.792
on a local newspaper.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.894
In Britain we have
national newspapers,

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:88% position:13%
we don't have syndicated
columns like you do.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:14.868 align:start position:0%
But I learned a local newspaper
in the suburbs of London

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:18.838 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then went to a magazine
and then went to The Guardian.

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:22.809
The Guardian is a bit like The
New York times, but more so,

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
it is the kind of
journalistic crucible

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:29.382 align:start size:84% position:16%
of left-wing
thinking in Britain.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.252 align:start size:81% position:19%
And at the time
that I went there,

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:37.157 align:start size:97% position:3%
I didn't ever really consider
myself to be left-wing,

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.526
but 'cause I wasn't
very ideological,

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.327
I consider myself
to be a liberal.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:42.896
Now I know that the word liberal

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.931
means something different
in America from Britain,

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
but what I meant by that,
what I mean by that,

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:50.770
was that I thought of myself
as an old fashioned liberal.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
That is to say
somebody who believes

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:58.144
in making a better world
by prioritizing the good

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:05.485
that people do over the bad,
standing up for the vulnerable,

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.453
against abuse of power,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:10.957 align:start size:84% position:16%
standing up for truth
rather than lies.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:13.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at that time I
thought that my colleagues

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.529
at The Guardian and in the left,

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:18.565
that we were all
on the same side

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.267 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we can talk
about this in detail.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.971 align:start size:97% position:3%
But nevertheless, over the
next few years I realized that

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.840
this was a big mistake, and
the while I still believed

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.177
in all those things, they
were on the other side,

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:97% position:3%
they were the people who
actually were the oppressors

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.949
of the poor and vulnerable.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:39.118
They were themselves
racist and antisemitic.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:43.122
And during this period,
which took 10, 20 years,

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:46.459
I changed also in the sense
that I became more aware

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:88% position:13%
of my Jewish background,
my Jewish identity,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.563
it became more important to me,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:55.235
and I became very, very
aware of the enormity

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:59.239
of the big lies being
told about Israel.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.941
Would you believe I'd
never been to Israel

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:05.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
and never wanted to go
until about the year 2000.

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.580
The year 2000 was the
first time I went,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.850 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I didn't particularly
like it for various reasons.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then within
two or three years,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:15.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
I had bought a
place in Jerusalem,

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.626
because my life and my
whole view of the world

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:21.894 align:start size:84% position:16%
and my view of myself
as a British Jew

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.296
had completely changed.

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:28.301 align:start size:97% position:3%
So that's a very short
thumbnail sketch of my descent

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:32.805
from being the kind of
a wise child of the left

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:36.109
to being the she-devil of
the Western Hemisphere.

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.712
- Yeah, well, I'm not sure how
much you know about my story,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:41.648
but I think a lot of
my audience is going,

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:43.650
"Dave, we've kind of
heard this before,"

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.917
because that in many ways,

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
although we're, we're
not the same age,

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.288
we're not from the same country.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:51.124 align:start size:97% position:3%
The story that you just
told of coming from the left

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
from a largely Jewish
secular family.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.361 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I mean, it's very
much the same story,

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.230 line:0%
and I think in many
ways our politics

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.067 line:0%
and the way you laid out,
what true liberalism is,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.335
really do line up.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.670
So can you talk a
little bit because

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.339
I get this question constantly.

00:05:06.339 --> 00:05:09.309
Now, can you talk
about when and why

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.911
you started to see the split

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:15.782
within the left towards
socialism, progressivism,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.016
whatever you wanna call it,

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.485 align:start size:88% position:13%
versus the liberalism
that you just described?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.890
- Yes, well, there was one
particular punctuation mark,

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.625
which really set
me on this path,

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:29.529
and it was in 1982 and it
was when in a conversation

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.164
with my colleagues
at The Guardian,

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:35.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was an editorial writer
and I thought of them

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:39.405
as being just like me, a
liberal in the best sense,

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:44.410
committed to truth and
reason and decent people.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we had a conversation
in which I was very troubled

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.850 align:start size:81% position:19%
by what at the
time seemed to me,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be the disproportionate
attention,

00:05:54.821 --> 00:05:59.025
being paid to what Israel was
doing in its war in Lebanon,

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.727
which was a controversial war,

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:03.896 align:start position:0%
but it was being portrayed
falsely as a war of aggression.

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.898
Whereas I knew,
and don't forget,

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.900 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'd never been to Israel and
didn't really want to go,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.102
and it wasn't really my thing,

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:12.472 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I knew that it
was trying to root out

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:14.407 align:start size:88% position:13%
the Palestinian
Liberation Organization,

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
stop it from
attacking Israelism,

00:06:17.043 --> 00:06:20.146 align:start size:88% position:13%
the PLO at that time
was in Southern Lebanon.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.548
But it was being represented
falsely as a war of aggression.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:26.085 align:start size:88% position:13%
And at the same time out
of the woodwork came,

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:29.455
unbridled antisemitism
that we British Jews

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:32.291 align:start position:0%
are all considered to be
basically all sticking together

00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:35.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a clannish kind of
way and defending Israel.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:38.164
And I was very troubled by
this and I was very troubled

00:06:38.164 --> 00:06:41.534
by the fact that The
Guardian was spending

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:45.304 align:start size:97% position:3%
such a disproportionate
amount of its time in hurling,

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:50.309
terrible obloquy at
Israel over all this.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:54.147 align:start size:97% position:3%
Whereas at the same time,
president Assad, the father,

00:06:54.147 --> 00:06:59.152 align:start size:97% position:3%
the current president
Assad had caused a massacre

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.487
of his political opponents,

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:05.825 align:start size:97% position:3%
something in between 15
and 40,000 of his opponents

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:08.761 align:start size:97% position:3%
were killed over the course
of a couple of weeks.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.630
And that story didn't really

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.131
have much traction
at The Guardian,

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.801
and I couldn't understand I
was different person then,

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.236
didn't really understand
what I was dealing with.

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:20.606
And I said to my colleagues,
one day in the editorial room,

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:24.110 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Why do we seem to have
a double standard?"

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.945
And there was a
terrible silence.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I realized at that moment
that I'd crossed a line.

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.983
I had no idea what the line
was or why I'd crossed it,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:34.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I realized I'd
stopped being one of them

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.856
and I'd become one of you.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:41.427 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they said, "Well, of
course, as a double standard,"

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:46.199
after all they said
to me, "Like you,"

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:49.735
and I became you and by
you, they meant Israel.

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:51.370
And I never been to Israel.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.807
"Like you, we in the West
are brought up to believe

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:57.477
in the sanctity of life,
respect for human rights,

00:07:57.477 --> 00:08:00.947 align:start size:97% position:3%
human dignity, whereas people
in the developing world

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:04.016 align:start size:97% position:3%
are not brought up to
believe any of those things.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:06.786
And so if they kill people,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:10.289 align:start size:84% position:16%
we cannot judge them
by our standards,

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:12.425
that would be racism."

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:14.827
And I thought, "What?"

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.929
And I said to them,
"What are you saying?

00:08:16.929 --> 00:08:20.766
That if one is unfortunate
enough to be born and bred

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:24.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
into the developing world,
then one does not then

00:08:24.437 --> 00:08:28.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
have the same rights to
life and liberty that we do,

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:31.577
to my mind, that's racism."

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:34.313
And they said, "Why
are you so upset?

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:37.049
We do you," and I
became you again,

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:42.054 align:start size:97% position:3%
"The great honor of assuming
that you are like us.

00:08:43.189 --> 00:08:44.790 align:start size:84% position:16%
You have the same
moral standards as us.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.795
And what's more you tell us
that you as the Jewish people

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.599
are morally superior to us."

00:08:53.599 --> 00:08:58.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now that is A, untrue and
B, it is sheer antisemitism.

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:03.276
And at that moment, I realized
that the assumption I'd made

00:09:03.276 --> 00:09:07.280 align:start size:97% position:3%
that we were all marching
under the same banner of truth

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.917
and freedom and decency
and all those good things

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:14.554
that was untrue, that I was
marching under that banner,

00:09:14.554 --> 00:09:18.758
but they were on the other
side, they, the liberals,

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:21.460 align:start size:84% position:16%
the left, the people
who assumed that

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.195
because they were the
liberals and the left,

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:27.033 align:start size:84% position:16%
they embodied virtue,
and everybody who
was not the liberals

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:30.703
and the left was a
bad and evil person.

00:09:30.703 --> 00:09:34.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were the racists,
they were the antisemites,

00:09:35.675 --> 00:09:38.578
and they believed in lies
and they were irrational.

00:09:38.578 --> 00:09:40.079
And from that moment,

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:42.481
I realized that there was
a difference between us.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:45.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
I couldn't any more
trust anything they said,

00:09:45.318 --> 00:09:47.987
but because I was very
attached to the left.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:52.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And because I hadn't quite
worked out in my mind

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:55.861
what had happened here, it
took me a while to realize

00:09:55.861 --> 00:09:58.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we were on different
sides completely.

00:09:58.731 --> 00:10:03.402
And how I realized it was that
I was writing as a columnist

00:10:03.402 --> 00:10:07.640
in the mid to late 80s
onwards, about issues,

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:10.543
a poem, which I fill up with
a left on every single one.

00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:13.112
So the first was 'Education'.

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:16.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
The second was the
'Breakdown of the Family'.

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:18.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first was the
'Breakdown of Education'.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:20.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
The second was the
'Breakdown of the Family'.

00:10:20.353 --> 00:10:23.723 align:start size:97% position:3%
The third was the 'Development
of Multiculturalism'

00:10:23.723 --> 00:10:27.426
and the erosion of the idea
that the Western Nation State

00:10:27.426 --> 00:10:29.929 align:start size:84% position:16%
was something that you
should be proud of.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we went from
there into 'Islamization',

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:35.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then into all
sorts of other stuff,

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:40.373 align:start position:0%
and issue by issue that liberal
world just fell in on me

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:46.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the moment I
started writing that,
I became considered,

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was told I had overnight
gone mad, insane.

00:10:52.551 --> 00:10:55.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
And overnight I had
changed my personality,

00:10:55.187 --> 00:10:59.025
like a kind of chameleon
into being right wing,

00:10:59.025 --> 00:11:01.661
very right wing,
ultra right wing,

00:11:01.661 --> 00:11:05.197
extremely right wing,
fascist, neofascist.

00:11:05.197 --> 00:11:09.301 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then as I started writing
about Israel, Zionist,

00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:11.103
a warmongering Zionist,

00:11:11.103 --> 00:11:15.508 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then a warmongering
Zionist insane right-wing Jew.

00:11:16.709 --> 00:11:19.145
And that's where I
kind of ended up.

00:11:19.145 --> 00:11:20.813
- Oh man, there's so much here.

00:11:21.947 --> 00:11:24.417
It's like hearing my
story just a, you know,

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.118
20 years in advance or
something like that.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:27.653 align:start size:84% position:16%
But so much of
what you're saying,

00:11:27.653 --> 00:11:32.491
I think is what now in 2020
millions of people worldwide

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:33.959
have woken up to.

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:36.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I have a couple of
followups there first off,

00:11:36.095 --> 00:11:38.931
what do you think is wrong?

00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:40.800
And I hate to say this
as someone that's still

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
considers myself a liberal
in that true sense,

00:11:43.502 --> 00:11:46.605
do you think there is an
inherent flaw in liberalism

00:11:46.605 --> 00:11:50.209 align:start size:88% position:13%
that has allowed
leftism and collectivism

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:51.777
to basically decimate it?

00:11:51.777 --> 00:11:54.213
So that there are
very few people

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:56.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
at this point in the
West, certainly in America

00:11:56.582 --> 00:11:59.151 align:start position:0%
who described themselves as
liberals the way we're talking,

00:11:59.151 --> 00:12:01.687 align:start size:97% position:3%
about it most of these, anyone
listening to this right now

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:05.257
would say, "Oh, they sound
mostly like conservatives.

00:12:05.257 --> 00:12:07.226
I probably come
off a little more

00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:09.628 align:start size:81% position:19%
on the libertarian
side of that."

00:12:09.628 --> 00:12:12.631 align:start size:84% position:16%
But do you think there
is an actual flaw

00:12:12.631 --> 00:12:14.900
in the good sense of liberalism

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:18.237
that allowed this monster in.

00:12:19.405 --> 00:12:23.309
Perhaps a protection
that conservatism has,

00:12:23.309 --> 00:12:24.877
that liberalism doesn't have?

00:12:25.978 --> 00:12:29.381 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Well, the fundamental
flaw in liberalism

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:35.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the way that it's
been developed is that...

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:37.089
Let's put it this way,

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:39.091
there are different
types of liberalism.

00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:42.294 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's the liberalism,
which comes out of,

00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:45.264 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would say conservatism
or other conservatism

00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:47.900 align:start size:84% position:16%
is a kind of defense
of liberalism.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:51.971
If you look up the, one of
the greatest philosophers

00:12:51.971 --> 00:12:54.673
of what's called conservatism,

00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:59.378
Edmund Burke in
the 18th century,

00:12:59.378 --> 00:13:01.347
now he's called a conservative.

00:13:01.347 --> 00:13:03.082
But what he reacted against

00:13:03.082 --> 00:13:05.084 align:start size:84% position:16%
was the French
Revolutionary terror.

00:13:05.084 --> 00:13:07.520 align:start size:84% position:16%
He understood that
the French Revolution,

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:11.290 align:start size:97% position:3%
which was supposedly all
about freeing the individual

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:16.295 align:start position:0%
and introducing the rule of
reason, divorced from religion.

00:13:17.396 --> 00:13:18.631
A whole lot of other stuff,

00:13:18.631 --> 00:13:20.299
but that's broadly
what it's about.

00:13:21.867 --> 00:13:23.803
It led directly to terror.

00:13:23.803 --> 00:13:26.739
So he reacted against
that, and as a result,

00:13:26.739 --> 00:13:28.207
he was called a conservative

00:13:28.207 --> 00:13:29.942 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's still a
called a conservative,

00:13:29.942 --> 00:13:32.311
he's called one of the
fathers of conservatism.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:33.779
But from where I'm standing,

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:37.516 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was actually defending
liberalism, he was different.

00:13:37.516 --> 00:13:38.751
What was he defending?

00:13:38.751 --> 00:13:41.253 align:start size:88% position:13%
He was defending
tolerance, and freedom,

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.888
and progress and reasoning.

00:13:42.888 --> 00:13:45.691
These are all things which
I associate with liberalism.

00:13:45.691 --> 00:13:48.694
Now liberalism has
a fundamental flaw,

00:13:48.694 --> 00:13:52.598
it is that it has two
fundamental flaws.

00:13:52.598 --> 00:13:57.069 align:start size:97% position:3%
One is that because it
prioritizes the individual,

00:14:00.873 --> 00:14:03.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
it has been
interpreted over time,

00:14:03.576 --> 00:14:05.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
and now in our
current time to mean

00:14:05.344 --> 00:14:09.648
that you can't then
establish any kind

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:11.584
of hierarchy of values.

00:14:11.584 --> 00:14:13.252
You can't say that
one set of values

00:14:13.252 --> 00:14:15.087
is better than anyone else's,

00:14:15.087 --> 00:14:18.991 align:start size:97% position:3%
because that's kind of being
nasty to somebody else.

00:14:18.991 --> 00:14:22.461
And consequently, the
logical flaw in that

00:14:22.461 --> 00:14:25.898
is that if you can't say
that anyone's lifestyle

00:14:25.898 --> 00:14:28.868
or culture is better
than anyone else's,

00:14:28.868 --> 00:14:30.836 align:start size:81% position:19%
then you can't say
that liberalism

00:14:30.836 --> 00:14:32.504
is better than anyone else's.

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:35.207
And consequently,
you can't defend

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:38.744 align:start size:97% position:3%
the fundamental liberal
values of freedom of speech,

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:41.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
and tolerance of
other points of view,

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:44.250 line:0%
and freedom of religion
and all those things,

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.352 line:0%
which make a liberal
tolerance society.

00:14:46.352 --> 00:14:47.586 line:0%
You can't defend them,

00:14:47.586 --> 00:14:50.022 line:0%
you can't defend the
equality of women.

00:14:50.022 --> 00:14:51.624
So when faced with say,

00:14:51.624 --> 00:14:54.460
the Islamic world
as a liberal today,

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:55.961
you cannot say that the West

00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:58.831 align:start size:81% position:19%
is better than
the Islamic world.

00:14:58.831 --> 00:15:03.636 align:start position:0%
Even though it is, because
surely the enslavement of women

00:15:03.636 --> 00:15:06.372
must be worse than
freedom for women,

00:15:06.372 --> 00:15:07.873
and equality for women.

00:15:07.873 --> 00:15:10.709
So that is one of the
essential, I think,

00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:12.278
contradictions in liberalism,

00:15:12.278 --> 00:15:15.281
that means that it's sort
of going down the plug,

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:20.286 align:start size:97% position:3%
plus the fact that it's
become a libertarian ideology,

00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:26.225
that is to say it's taken
the notion of the dignity

00:15:26.225 --> 00:15:28.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the individual and
respect for the individual

00:15:28.427 --> 00:15:30.829
in my view is at the
heart of liberalism.

00:15:32.298 --> 00:15:36.535
But in my view, that can only
be enshrined by paradoxically,

00:15:36.535 --> 00:15:40.372
a body of laws and moral
values that are regarded

00:15:40.372 --> 00:15:42.641
as kind of binding on you.

00:15:42.641 --> 00:15:46.578 align:start size:97% position:3%
But if you detach the
individual from those laws,

00:15:46.578 --> 00:15:48.380
then you get a kind
of free for all.

00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:51.350
And once you have
a free for all,

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:54.787 align:start size:84% position:16%
then it's everyone out
for him or herself.

00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:59.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then you have the
strong dominating the weak,

00:15:59.725 --> 00:16:02.561
and then you get to a
situation very fast,

00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:04.196
which is where we've got to,

00:16:04.196 --> 00:16:06.966
where you don't have
a liberal society.

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:10.569 align:start size:88% position:13%
You have a tremendously
illiberal society,

00:16:10.569 --> 00:16:12.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's made even
worse by the fact

00:16:12.871 --> 00:16:15.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
that this kind of liberalism
or I would call it,

00:16:15.708 --> 00:16:19.878 align:start size:84% position:16%
libertarianism is
actually an ideology.

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:21.113
Now what's an ideology?

00:16:21.113 --> 00:16:25.284
An ideology is where
the power of the idea

00:16:25.284 --> 00:16:28.554
must trumps everything else.

00:16:28.554 --> 00:16:32.391
You can't ever say,
the idea is wrong.

00:16:32.391 --> 00:16:35.561
So if you come along with a
load of facts and you say,

00:16:35.561 --> 00:16:39.098
"Well, this idea is wrong
because here are the facts.

00:16:39.098 --> 00:16:41.800 align:start size:88% position:13%
Here's the evidence
that shows it's wrong."

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:44.737 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, the ideology
says, you must be wrong.

00:16:44.737 --> 00:16:47.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
There can be no challenge
to the ideology.

00:16:47.639 --> 00:16:51.143 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so you have to be stopped,
you have to be suppressed,

00:16:51.143 --> 00:16:53.846
because the ideology
of liberalism is that

00:16:53.846 --> 00:16:56.348
it's bound up with the
betterment of humanity,

00:16:56.348 --> 00:16:58.117
the perfection of the world.

00:16:58.117 --> 00:17:01.553 align:start size:97% position:3%
So anyone who stands against
that, isn't just wrong,

00:17:01.553 --> 00:17:04.923
they're actually evil,
and if they're evil,

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:06.859
they have to be stopped.

00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:09.061
And so you have this
phenomenon in which

00:17:09.061 --> 00:17:12.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have people who
purport to be liberal,

00:17:12.264 --> 00:17:16.902
who are stamping out free
expression on our campuses,

00:17:16.902 --> 00:17:19.438
preventing people from speaking,

00:17:19.438 --> 00:17:23.409 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is absolutely
the absolute antithesis

00:17:23.409 --> 00:17:24.877
of true liberal values.

00:17:24.877 --> 00:17:27.079 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's the
paradox of liberalism,

00:17:27.079 --> 00:17:30.649 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's become an
illiberal ideology.

00:17:30.649 --> 00:17:34.119 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Melanie, you would
absolutely love my book.

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:37.156 align:start position:0%
So I'm going to get your
address after and send it to you

00:17:37.156 --> 00:17:39.825
because I'm making many
of the same arguments

00:17:39.825 --> 00:17:43.829
and that connection between
between truly being liberal

00:17:43.829 --> 00:17:45.964
and having something
outside of yourself,

00:17:45.964 --> 00:17:48.300
which I think we're gonna
get to in a little bit.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.501
But I wanna back for a second,

00:17:49.501 --> 00:17:51.303
because you said
that you grew up

00:17:51.303 --> 00:17:53.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a secular Jewish
household that was similar

00:17:53.472 --> 00:17:55.974 align:start size:81% position:19%
to most of the
others in the 50s.

00:17:55.974 --> 00:17:58.710 align:start size:88% position:13%
Can you sort of describe
what does that mean?

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.313
And one of the questions
I get all the time now is,

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:03.048
what happened to the Jews?

00:18:03.048 --> 00:18:05.284
How did the Jews
all become lefties?

00:18:05.284 --> 00:18:09.688
When the left has become
so rabidly, anti-Jewish,

00:18:09.688 --> 00:18:12.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
anti-Israel, anti-liberal
all of those things.

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.626
I mean, I think you
can probably trace

00:18:14.626 --> 00:18:16.128
a pretty clean thread on that,

00:18:16.128 --> 00:18:17.563
but can you first describe
what did it mean to grow up

00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:19.731
in a secular Jewish household?

00:18:19.731 --> 00:18:21.700
Because I think that
confuses some people

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.236
and then sort of the road
that that takes us on.

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:27.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, well, to make
people even more confused,

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:29.074
it wasn't what I would
call strictly speaking,

00:18:29.074 --> 00:18:30.609
a secular household.

00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:33.745
I mean, certainly a highly
Orthodox observant people

00:18:33.745 --> 00:18:34.947
might well call it that.

00:18:34.947 --> 00:18:37.116
But, I didn't think
of it like that.

00:18:37.116 --> 00:18:39.785
My parents belong to
an Orthodox synagogue,

00:18:39.785 --> 00:18:42.488 align:start size:84% position:16%
they went to synagogue
three times a year,

00:18:42.488 --> 00:18:46.191 align:start size:88% position:13%
the two days of Rosh
Hashanah and Yom Kippur.

00:18:46.191 --> 00:18:49.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
We did not observe the Shabbat
in that my parents worked,

00:18:50.596 --> 00:18:53.432 align:start size:88% position:13%
they were modest people,
they had to work,

00:18:53.432 --> 00:18:55.734
or they felt they had to work,

00:18:55.734 --> 00:19:00.606
but we were kosher really
kosher at home and out.

00:19:02.074 --> 00:19:06.812
And we had a Friday night meal
with candles and Kiddush and,

00:19:09.014 --> 00:19:11.717
you know, I didn't go out,
but we had the television on.

00:19:11.717 --> 00:19:13.919
It was that kind of upbringing.

00:19:13.919 --> 00:19:17.022
And, you know, my parents
they were modest people.

00:19:17.022 --> 00:19:20.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
They weren't educated
people, but my mother was,

00:19:21.293 --> 00:19:23.128
she had a kind of
religious instinct

00:19:24.363 --> 00:19:27.733
and she had very, very
strong moral values,

00:19:27.733 --> 00:19:30.736 align:start size:88% position:13%
which I came to
recognize in later years

00:19:30.736 --> 00:19:32.538
were actually Jewish values.

00:19:32.538 --> 00:19:34.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, I was
when I was a little girl.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.777 align:start size:97% position:3%
I remember every night,
she said the Shema with me,

00:19:38.777 --> 00:19:42.414
the fundamental prayer
of the Jewish religion.

00:19:42.414 --> 00:19:43.949
She said it with me every night.

00:19:43.949 --> 00:19:47.319
So I wouldn't describe it as
a secular Jewish household,

00:19:47.319 --> 00:19:51.089 align:start position:0%
but it certainly, wasn't a very
observant Jewish household.

00:19:51.089 --> 00:19:52.457
Now what happened to the Jews?

00:19:52.457 --> 00:19:53.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, you see,
there's a difference

00:19:53.692 --> 00:19:56.795
between the Jewish
community in Britain,

00:19:56.795 --> 00:19:59.198 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Jewish
community in America.

00:19:59.198 --> 00:20:02.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jewish ministry in
America, as, I don't know,

00:20:02.501 --> 00:20:05.737
you said you, is not
only mainly Democrat,

00:20:05.737 --> 00:20:06.905
but the same proportion

00:20:08.106 --> 00:20:11.810
are non traditional
non Orthodox Jews.

00:20:13.245 --> 00:20:17.749
And in America, it seems to
me, the prevailing and wisdom

00:20:18.817 --> 00:20:20.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the Jewish
community in America,

00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:22.454 align:start size:84% position:16%
who are the majority
and the majority

00:20:22.454 --> 00:20:23.722
of them are not Orthodox,

00:20:23.722 --> 00:20:26.491
is to assume that's
the secular ideology

00:20:26.491 --> 00:20:29.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
we've been talking about,
which actually is anti-Jewish,

00:20:29.928 --> 00:20:32.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's fundamentally
anti the Hebrew Bible.

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:35.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
It sets out to undermine
all the basic presets

00:20:35.701 --> 00:20:37.603
of the Hebrew Bible.

00:20:37.603 --> 00:20:41.440
The American Jews, the 70%
who are progressively minded

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:45.644 align:start size:88% position:13%
or secular, they've
told themselves there's
a Jewish values.

00:20:45.644 --> 00:20:47.346 align:start size:84% position:16%
They've kind of
squared the circle.

00:20:47.346 --> 00:20:49.381
They can be good Jews
and believe in stuff,

00:20:49.381 --> 00:20:50.849
which is basically anti-Jew.

00:20:52.017 --> 00:20:54.853
Now that's disastrous
for American Jews.

00:20:54.853 --> 00:20:56.088
I don't need to tell you,

00:20:56.088 --> 00:20:58.490 align:start size:84% position:16%
but in Britain it's
very different.

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.827
In Britain, something
like between 60 and 70%

00:21:01.827 --> 00:21:06.665
of British Jews have for the
last several general elections

00:21:06.665 --> 00:21:08.767 align:start size:84% position:16%
voted for the
Conservative Party.

00:21:08.767 --> 00:21:10.335 align:start size:88% position:13%
They are not the
equivalent politically,

00:21:10.335 --> 00:21:13.171
your Democrats at all.

00:21:13.171 --> 00:21:16.708
But they voted for the
conservative party mainly

00:21:16.708 --> 00:21:19.611
through their sort of
pocket book, really.

00:21:19.611 --> 00:21:21.113
But they have at the same time,

00:21:21.113 --> 00:21:23.181 align:start size:88% position:13%
like so many
conservatives in Britain

00:21:23.181 --> 00:21:24.883 align:start size:88% position:13%
and so many
Republicans in America,

00:21:24.883 --> 00:21:29.454
they've kind of absorbed
like a kind of osmosis,

00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:31.323 align:start size:81% position:19%
the prevailing
liberal and wisdom

00:21:31.323 --> 00:21:33.925
about a whole range
of cultural issues.

00:21:33.925 --> 00:21:35.127
But they're not very political,

00:21:35.127 --> 00:21:36.561
they're not very
ideological at all.

00:21:36.561 --> 00:21:39.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they're quite different
from American Jews.

00:21:39.331 --> 00:21:43.168 align:start size:81% position:19%
However, the rates
of assimilation

00:21:43.168 --> 00:21:45.203
in Britain are pretty awful.

00:21:47.472 --> 00:21:50.876 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, more and more
people are just dropping out

00:21:50.876 --> 00:21:52.277
from Judaism, altogether,

00:21:52.277 --> 00:21:55.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, belonging to
progressive denominations

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:58.216
where their children
marry out non Jews.

00:21:58.216 --> 00:22:00.585
And they themselves drop out.

00:22:00.585 --> 00:22:03.522
But it's more a
kind of a process

00:22:03.522 --> 00:22:07.492 align:start size:84% position:16%
of sort of
demographic attrition,

00:22:07.492 --> 00:22:10.295 align:start size:88% position:13%
rather than the
embrace of an ideology,

00:22:10.295 --> 00:22:12.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is actually
inimical to Judaism,

00:22:12.431 --> 00:22:15.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is I think
what characterizes so
many American Jews.

00:22:17.269 --> 00:22:19.338 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Okay, so there's
many directions

00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:20.939
we could go from there,

00:22:22.207 --> 00:22:23.975 align:start position:0%
if we were to sum up
everything we're talking about,

00:22:23.975 --> 00:22:28.847 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you see what is happening
across the world right now,

00:22:28.847 --> 00:22:32.417
and how liberalism
has sort of failed.

00:22:32.417 --> 00:22:34.853
And what that then
probably leads to

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:38.623
is sort of some version of
right wing authoritarianism

00:22:38.623 --> 00:22:41.393
or something like that, if
you agree with that premise.

00:22:42.794 --> 00:22:46.231
What can we do if you want
to save liberalism right now?

00:22:46.231 --> 00:22:47.632
What can people do?

00:22:49.101 --> 00:22:53.572 align:start position:0%
- Well, it's this paradox,
again, that to save liberalism,

00:22:53.572 --> 00:22:56.208
you have to be conservative.

00:22:57.376 --> 00:23:00.879
And I do believe
that the problem

00:23:02.247 --> 00:23:05.550
that the sort of death
throes of liberalism

00:23:06.952 --> 00:23:09.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
have been caused, not just
by the what's happened

00:23:09.721 --> 00:23:13.058 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the left or the progressive
circles in the West,

00:23:13.058 --> 00:23:16.228
but by the fact that the
people who are supposedly

00:23:16.228 --> 00:23:19.431
to who are supposed to
be defending the West,

00:23:19.431 --> 00:23:22.000
against this onslaught,

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:25.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
have thrown in the
towel a long time ago,

00:23:25.404 --> 00:23:27.205
largely through ignorance.

00:23:29.541 --> 00:23:32.944
There are not precise parallels

00:23:32.944 --> 00:23:36.014 align:start size:97% position:3%
between British conservatives
and American Republicans,

00:23:36.014 --> 00:23:37.949
but nevertheless,
there are certain,

00:23:37.949 --> 00:23:41.653
I think, constant
characteristics,

00:23:41.653 --> 00:23:44.756 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the conservative
wing of politics,

00:23:44.756 --> 00:23:47.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I can put it that way,
(clears throat)

00:23:47.492 --> 00:23:50.629
has forgotten what it is
in business to conserve.

00:23:52.097 --> 00:23:56.234
And especially, I think since
the fall of the Soviet Union,

00:23:57.369 --> 00:23:59.171
which I think was taking place

00:23:59.171 --> 00:24:02.307
before the Berlin wall
actually fell, you know,

00:24:02.307 --> 00:24:05.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Soviet union
clearly was, you know,

00:24:05.076 --> 00:24:07.913
in its death throes for
a long time before that.

00:24:07.913 --> 00:24:09.681
And I think that
what happened was,

00:24:11.116 --> 00:24:14.986
that conservatively
minded individuals

00:24:14.986 --> 00:24:17.656
or conservative politicians,

00:24:17.656 --> 00:24:20.091
the conservative
political class,

00:24:20.091 --> 00:24:23.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the Soviet Union
fell, it sort of thought,

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:27.199 align:start size:88% position:13%
"Oh, our fox has been
shot, what do we do now?

00:24:27.199 --> 00:24:28.900
We've won."

00:24:28.900 --> 00:24:31.336
Here is, you know, the Soviet
Union having disintegrated,

00:24:31.336 --> 00:24:34.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
is no longer a threat,
everyone's bought
into the market.

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:36.641
Now, the problem
with conservatives

00:24:36.641 --> 00:24:40.278 align:start position:0%
is that they tend to think
entirely in terms of economics.

00:24:41.446 --> 00:24:43.348
They don't think in
terms of culture,

00:24:43.348 --> 00:24:45.817
they don't understand what
Edmund Burke understood,

00:24:45.817 --> 00:24:47.052
during the French Revolution.

00:24:47.052 --> 00:24:49.187
It's all about culture,
it's all about values,

00:24:49.187 --> 00:24:51.089
it's all about moral values,
they didn't think like that.

00:24:51.089 --> 00:24:53.124 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they haven't
done that for years.

00:24:53.124 --> 00:24:55.260 align:start size:88% position:13%
So they thought, "Well,
what do we do now?

00:24:55.260 --> 00:24:56.962
Everyone's bought
into the market,

00:24:56.962 --> 00:25:00.665
what are we going to
hang our hat on now?"

00:25:00.665 --> 00:25:03.568
And they alighted upon freedom.

00:25:03.568 --> 00:25:04.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I remember this
happening at the time.

00:25:04.903 --> 00:25:09.241
And I thought, "Oh
no, they've had it.

00:25:09.241 --> 00:25:10.842
This is ridiculous because

00:25:10.842 --> 00:25:13.778
the left hung its
hat on freedom."

00:25:13.778 --> 00:25:17.182
So what happened was that
while the left venerated

00:25:17.182 --> 00:25:21.887
and worshiped the shrine of
personal individual freedom.

00:25:21.887 --> 00:25:26.525 line:0%
Freedom to do exactly what
I like, behaviors I like,

00:25:26.525 --> 00:25:27.759 line:0%
had the values that I like,

00:25:27.759 --> 00:25:30.595 line:0%
and no one can tell
me that I'm wrong.

00:25:30.595 --> 00:25:34.799 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Conservatives said
that everything that's
good in the world

00:25:34.799 --> 00:25:37.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
is going to be delivered
by the free market.

00:25:38.336 --> 00:25:41.540 align:start size:97% position:3%
And consequently, the
conservatives did not realize

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:43.542
what was happening on
the cultural front.

00:25:43.542 --> 00:25:47.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
They didn't realize that
education was being redefined

00:25:47.312 --> 00:25:48.813 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the transmission
of a culture

00:25:48.813 --> 00:25:51.449
down through the generations
to teaching your children,

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:54.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
that your culture
was fundamentally
illegitimate, racist,

00:25:54.619 --> 00:25:56.454
and should be obliterated.

00:25:56.454 --> 00:25:58.590
They didn't realize
that was going on.

00:25:58.590 --> 00:26:03.361
They didn't realize that the
freedom to junk your husband,

00:26:03.361 --> 00:26:06.865
the freedom to have a
baby without a father,

00:26:06.865 --> 00:26:08.066
even without the baby

00:26:08.066 --> 00:26:09.734
even knowing who his father was,

00:26:09.734 --> 00:26:11.236
and perhaps you didn't
even know who father was.

00:26:11.236 --> 00:26:14.706
That that freedom would
come with a terrible cost

00:26:14.706 --> 00:26:18.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the child and to the
woman and also to the man.

00:26:18.376 --> 00:26:20.145
They didn't figure all that out

00:26:20.145 --> 00:26:21.846
and all sorts of other stuff.

00:26:21.846 --> 00:26:26.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they just lost the plot
and then having vacated

00:26:28.219 --> 00:26:30.288 align:start position:0%
the cultural battleground,
they then observed that society

00:26:30.288 --> 00:26:31.790
was changing in that direction.

00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:35.961 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they said, "Oh, we can't
do anything to stop this.

00:26:35.961 --> 00:26:38.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like Knute
holding back the tide.

00:26:38.496 --> 00:26:42.033 align:start size:88% position:13%
We must go with the flow
of cultural change."

00:26:42.033 --> 00:26:44.703
And so they became
part of the problem.

00:26:44.703 --> 00:26:48.707 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's why
liberalism was allowed

00:26:48.707 --> 00:26:51.543 align:start size:97% position:3%
to become the kind of
monster that it has become,

00:26:51.543 --> 00:26:55.413 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is illiberalism
or as somebody

00:26:55.413 --> 00:26:58.016 align:start size:84% position:16%
who was a very
distinguished thinker

00:26:58.016 --> 00:27:00.452 align:start size:84% position:16%
once coined the term
and it's so true,

00:27:00.452 --> 00:27:04.456
cultural totalitarianism is
what we're living through.

00:27:04.456 --> 00:27:05.957
- My friend, Michael Malice

00:27:05.957 --> 00:27:07.559
who's a brilliant
political thinker,

00:27:07.559 --> 00:27:10.428
he's more of like
a anarchist type,

00:27:10.428 --> 00:27:14.265 align:start size:97% position:3%
but he says that conservatism
is just liberalism

00:27:14.265 --> 00:27:17.335 align:start size:88% position:13%
at the speed limit,
which I think is partly

00:27:17.335 --> 00:27:18.970
what you're getting to there.

00:27:18.970 --> 00:27:21.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you sense that something
has shifted though?

00:27:21.640 --> 00:27:25.377 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because I do sense right
now that it's partly

00:27:25.377 --> 00:27:28.513
because of Trump may be
90% because of Trump,

00:27:28.513 --> 00:27:30.849
although maybe Trump is
just a symptom of it,

00:27:30.849 --> 00:27:32.817 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that conservatives
have started

00:27:32.817 --> 00:27:35.253
to understand the cultural part.

00:27:35.253 --> 00:27:37.989
I think there is a sense
of, if you look online,

00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:41.493 align:start position:0%
the things that are fun and
funny and the memes and comedy,

00:27:41.493 --> 00:27:43.828 align:start size:84% position:16%
the left has destroyed
all of these things

00:27:43.828 --> 00:27:45.764
through it's totalitarian view,

00:27:45.764 --> 00:27:48.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the things that are
actually interesting right now

00:27:48.767 --> 00:27:52.003
are things that are coming out
of more right leaning circles

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:56.141 align:start position:0%
do you credit Trump for breaking
through that thing in a way

00:27:56.141 --> 00:27:59.411
that the conservatives would
have never done otherwise?

00:27:59.411 --> 00:28:04.349 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think the election of
Donald Trump was the outcome

00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:08.486
of a change that had
already taken place.

00:28:08.486 --> 00:28:13.158
That is to say, I think that
there were two shoes that fell.

00:28:13.158 --> 00:28:16.161 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's not the right
metaphor in 2016.

00:28:16.161 --> 00:28:17.862 align:start size:81% position:19%
One was the Brexit
vote in Britain

00:28:17.862 --> 00:28:20.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the other was the
election of Donald Trump.

00:28:20.298 --> 00:28:22.834
And on both occasions,
I think what happened

00:28:22.834 --> 00:28:26.271
or that obviously they're
very different phenomena,

00:28:26.271 --> 00:28:29.941
different countries, but they
were fueled by the same thing,

00:28:29.941 --> 00:28:33.611
which was that the vast
bulk of ordinary people,

00:28:33.611 --> 00:28:35.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
the millions and millions
and millions of...

00:28:35.413 --> 00:28:38.116
when I say ordinary people,
I mean the kind of people

00:28:38.116 --> 00:28:42.587
who don't have typically a
higher university education,

00:28:43.922 --> 00:28:48.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
and who had spent
decades being preached at

00:28:50.061 --> 00:28:54.332
and being scorned and being
vilified and being traduced

00:28:55.800 --> 00:28:58.536
by the intelligence here,
which dominates completely

00:28:58.536 --> 00:29:01.506
the universities and the media

00:29:01.506 --> 00:29:03.842 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the whole
cultural operators.

00:29:03.842 --> 00:29:06.544
And more than that,
dominated politics

00:29:06.544 --> 00:29:09.247 align:start size:84% position:16%
because even so-called
conservatives,

00:29:09.247 --> 00:29:10.749
the Conservative
Party in Britain,

00:29:10.749 --> 00:29:14.018 align:start size:97% position:3%
the Republicans in America,
didn't really differ that much

00:29:14.018 --> 00:29:18.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
in this cultural
issues from the left.

00:29:18.356 --> 00:29:21.392 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they were all basically
saying to the people,

00:29:21.392 --> 00:29:22.794
"You don't know what
you're talking about.

00:29:22.794 --> 00:29:25.263
You're just rednecks,
you're just stupid.

00:29:25.263 --> 00:29:26.965
You don't even have a
university education.

00:29:26.965 --> 00:29:31.870 align:start size:97% position:3%
You're bigoted, you don't like
immigrants, you're racist."

00:29:31.870 --> 00:29:36.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
So the things that
ordinary people value,

00:29:36.141 --> 00:29:37.742
which is community,

00:29:37.742 --> 00:29:40.178 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is the attachment
to their country,

00:29:40.178 --> 00:29:42.380
patriotism love
of their country.

00:29:42.380 --> 00:29:45.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the kind of
instinctive understanding

00:29:45.116 --> 00:29:48.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
that a country and a
culture is made up of people

00:29:48.653 --> 00:29:50.655
who share your own values.

00:29:50.655 --> 00:29:52.991
They don't have
to look like you,

00:29:52.991 --> 00:29:55.059
they can be different
color faces from you.

00:29:55.059 --> 00:29:57.028 align:start size:97% position:3%
They can be a different
ethnic backgrounds from you,

00:29:57.028 --> 00:29:59.731
but at some important juncture,

00:29:59.731 --> 00:30:02.600
they share the most
important values

00:30:02.600 --> 00:30:04.702
of that society
and that culture,

00:30:04.702 --> 00:30:07.138 align:start size:84% position:16%
which means that
you're all basically

00:30:07.138 --> 00:30:09.707 align:start size:84% position:16%
sharing the same
cultural experience.

00:30:09.707 --> 00:30:11.242 align:start size:84% position:16%
You're all attached
to the nation.

00:30:11.242 --> 00:30:13.845
You all understand
what it means to you.

00:30:13.845 --> 00:30:17.615
Now that understanding
that cultural attachment

00:30:17.615 --> 00:30:20.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
was vilified as
racist and xenophobic

00:30:20.919 --> 00:30:24.622 align:start size:88% position:13%
by virtually the
entire political class.

00:30:24.622 --> 00:30:29.327
And when Brexit happened, it
was this monumental revolt

00:30:29.327 --> 00:30:34.199
by all those millions who said,
we've been given a vote now,

00:30:34.199 --> 00:30:38.169
and we can now use this
vote for this issue.

00:30:38.169 --> 00:30:41.005
We want our country
and our culture back.

00:30:41.005 --> 00:30:44.642 align:start size:88% position:13%
And they voted to leave
the European Union

00:30:44.642 --> 00:30:49.614 align:start size:97% position:3%
and restore Britain as an
independent democratic nation

00:30:50.849 --> 00:30:53.084
governing itself for the
first time for decades.

00:30:53.084 --> 00:30:56.287
And when that happened on
that morning of that vote,

00:30:56.287 --> 00:31:00.625
when I woke up and realized
that that vote had happened,

00:31:00.625 --> 00:31:02.427
I had two thoughts.

00:31:02.427 --> 00:31:07.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
The first thought
was, "Oh my goodness,

00:31:08.800 --> 00:31:12.503 align:start size:97% position:3%
there is a chance that Britain
can survive after all."

00:31:13.905 --> 00:31:16.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my second thought was,
"The intelligence here

00:31:16.875 --> 00:31:19.611
will never allow it to happen."

00:31:19.611 --> 00:31:22.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
And for the following
three years,

00:31:22.013 --> 00:31:25.717 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have this titanic
fight in Britain

00:31:25.717 --> 00:31:27.685
to reverse the Brexit vote.

00:31:27.685 --> 00:31:28.853
And then a few months later,

00:31:28.853 --> 00:31:30.488 align:start size:84% position:16%
the election of
Donald Trump happened,

00:31:30.488 --> 00:31:32.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then America it seemed
to me your intelligence

00:31:32.924 --> 00:31:36.127
or your political class had
a very similar reaction,

00:31:36.127 --> 00:31:39.497
but rather more, I would
say violently expressed

00:31:39.497 --> 00:31:41.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
rather than were
extremely expressed.

00:31:41.666 --> 00:31:43.268
But nevertheless,
the same thing,

00:31:43.268 --> 00:31:44.869
how could this have happened?

00:31:44.869 --> 00:31:46.437
This can't be true.

00:31:46.437 --> 00:31:47.839
This can't have happened.

00:31:47.839 --> 00:31:50.742
The people are stupid.
The people got it wrong.

00:31:50.742 --> 00:31:53.978
We have been robbed of
our natural inheritance,

00:31:53.978 --> 00:31:57.782
which is a democratic
presidency in eternity.

00:31:57.782 --> 00:32:01.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they didn't understand
and would not accept

00:32:01.586 --> 00:32:03.421
that the people
had got it right.

00:32:03.421 --> 00:32:05.423
The people wanted
their country back.

00:32:05.423 --> 00:32:07.458
They wanted, again,
the rule of law,

00:32:07.458 --> 00:32:10.595 align:start size:88% position:13%
they wanted immigration
to be enforced

00:32:10.595 --> 00:32:13.798
so that they would
again have borders.

00:32:13.798 --> 00:32:16.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
That meant something
without borders,

00:32:16.334 --> 00:32:18.403
you cannot have a nation.

00:32:18.403 --> 00:32:20.305 align:start size:84% position:16%
They didn't want
their cultural values

00:32:20.305 --> 00:32:22.774
trashed the whole time.

00:32:22.774 --> 00:32:25.043
They didn't want to
be told that America

00:32:25.043 --> 00:32:27.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
was the rogue
state of the world.

00:32:27.312 --> 00:32:29.480
They wanted to be
told that America

00:32:29.480 --> 00:32:32.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
was the exceptional
nation again.

00:32:32.317 --> 00:32:34.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that America stood
for values of which

00:32:34.385 --> 00:32:36.821
they could be proud of
which they would want

00:32:36.821 --> 00:32:39.791
to have other people emulate.

00:32:39.791 --> 00:32:42.093
That's what they wanted when
they voted for Donald Trump.

00:32:42.093 --> 00:32:44.462 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now, what ever you think
about Donald Trump,

00:32:44.462 --> 00:32:49.434
whatever you think about him,
that is what people voted for.

00:32:49.434 --> 00:32:51.636
And, you know, ever since we've,

00:32:51.636 --> 00:32:55.106
you've had this
tremendous fight,

00:32:55.106 --> 00:32:58.776
this tremendous fight to
get that man out of office

00:32:58.776 --> 00:33:01.479 align:start size:88% position:13%
by hook or by crook,
and it's the same thing,

00:33:01.479 --> 00:33:06.484
it's the class who feel that
not only are they entitled

00:33:07.919 --> 00:33:11.756
to rule according to their own
lights and their own values,

00:33:11.756 --> 00:33:15.660
but that it's a kind of
offense against nature

00:33:15.660 --> 00:33:19.130
that they shouldn't do
so, and they have to,

00:33:19.130 --> 00:33:20.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
they have some
kind of moral duty.

00:33:20.732 --> 00:33:24.602 align:start size:97% position:3%
They feel they have a moral
duty to reverse Brexit

00:33:24.602 --> 00:33:26.738
to get Trump out of office.

00:33:26.738 --> 00:33:29.807
And so that's where we are,

00:33:29.807 --> 00:33:32.543 align:start size:84% position:16%
the fight is
absolutely still on.

00:33:32.543 --> 00:33:34.812
And who knows how
it's going to end?

00:33:34.812 --> 00:33:37.482
I do not know how it's
going to end obviously.

00:33:37.482 --> 00:33:41.686
And also I think that, you
know, even if Brexit happens,

00:33:41.686 --> 00:33:45.356
I say even if, because
even now, I'm not sure,

00:33:46.524 --> 00:33:48.192
although it looks
as if we, you know,

00:33:48.192 --> 00:33:53.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
Britain is going to finally
slouch off the embrace,

00:33:54.065 --> 00:33:55.600
the deadly embrace of the EU.

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:58.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even if president Trump
were to get elected

00:33:58.002 --> 00:34:00.705
for a second term, I
would not be confident

00:34:00.705 --> 00:34:03.441
that the West would survive.

00:34:03.441 --> 00:34:05.877
But at least there
would be a chance.

00:34:05.877 --> 00:34:07.812
At least there'll
be a chance because

00:34:07.812 --> 00:34:11.682 align:start size:84% position:16%
if the left gets power
again in America,

00:34:11.682 --> 00:34:14.419 align:start size:81% position:19%
or if Britain were
not to be able

00:34:14.419 --> 00:34:17.488 align:start size:97% position:3%
to become an independent
self-governing nation again,

00:34:17.488 --> 00:34:20.158 align:start size:84% position:16%
be no chance, no
chance whatsoever that

00:34:20.158 --> 00:34:23.061 align:start size:88% position:13%
it could ever reinstate
these countries

00:34:23.061 --> 00:34:24.395
and the culture they present

00:34:24.395 --> 00:34:26.931
could ever reassert
themselves totally.

00:34:26.931 --> 00:34:30.501 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, got it, it's a
dire warning, but you know,

00:34:30.501 --> 00:34:33.037
I'm basically with
you, this is it.

00:34:33.037 --> 00:34:36.040 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's sort of like the
grand fight all the decades

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:39.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
of indoctrinating youth
and destroying institutions

00:34:39.444 --> 00:34:43.514
and everything else, it has
